 "notes": {
  "intro": {
   "fill": "purple",
   "page": "overview",
   "w": 440,
   "x": -1000,
   "y": 0,
   "text": "deploy.local, agent-first. Scout keeps the dev loop moving; Warden watches apps and computers. Light work runs free on SER (Qwen3-8B on Lemonade); code and review use Claude and Codex. Every screen loads the deploy.local design system (Theme menu)."
  },
  "desktop": {
   "fill": "purple",
   "page": "start",
   "w": 440,
   "x": -1000,
   "y": 0,
   "text": "Desktop app: Electron on Mac, Linux and Windows; iOS stays SwiftUI. The window loads deploy.local from your coordinator, trusting only its CA. The shell adds the menu bar or tray, notifications, a login item, the bundled worker (installing the app adds a computer) and the native control helper for screen use. It notifies only for Waiting on you items and failing apps."
  },
  "cli": {
   "fill": "purple",
   "page": "cli",
   "w": 440,
   "x": -1000,
   "y": 0,
   "text": "CLI proposal. Today bin/deploy.js is one 3,389-line file with 36 command lines and 25 global options. Proposed: six groups in the app's words, [app] as an optional positional, steps instead of log dumps, the dark theme's palette, --json everywhere and exit code 3 while something waits on you. Old commands keep working for one release."
  },
  "build": {
   "fill": "purple",
   "page": "overview",
   "w": 440,
   "x": -1000,
   "y": 420,
   "text": "Build rules for v2: the server sends each conversation as typed events (decision, work log, task link, answer, report) and every client renders them, folding but never dropping a decision. Tabs appear only once their thing exists. Words are taught once, where they first happen. Agents brief once a day and otherwise speak only when needed."
  },
